From 4daa36002f8a9bff19135661d9c9cf98723f7392 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudy Cato <rudy@americanfoodbeverage.local>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:32:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Inventory: item description, warehouse/aisle/bin
 location, min qty, removed/returned tracking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Product: new description field (separate from the short catalog name)
- Inventory: new warehouse, aisle, bin_column fields (structured location,
  replacing the single free-text location for editing purposes; location
  string kept in sync automatically for anything still reading it)
- New PATCH /inventory/{id}/location endpoint — edit warehouse/aisle/bin
  and min qty (reorder_threshold) independent of quantity adjustments
- InventoryReason: added 'removed' and 'returned' — sign is enforced
  server-side (removed always subtracts, returned always adds) regardless
  of what a client sends, so it can't be inverted by mistake
- Dashboard inventory table: added Description and Location columns, plus
  Location and History action buttons per row
- New Location modal (edit warehouse/aisle/bin/min qty) and History modal
  (full transaction log per item — received/removed/returned/adjusted)
- Adjust modal: reason dropdown now includes Removed and Returned, with
  a note explaining the auto-sign behavior
- seed.py: populates realistic warehouse/aisle/bin data (catalog items in
  aisles A-N by category, packaging/PPE in a separate 'Supplies' warehouse)
  and auto-generated descriptions
